---
<Base
  title="Business Plan"
  description="The Leaf & Lantern business plan: concept, market analysis, operations, financial model, brand system, and development roadmap."
>
  <div class="progress-track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="progress-bar" id="progress"></div></div>

  <header class="plan-hero">
    <div class="container plan-hero-inner">
      <span class="plan-kicker">Concept & Feasibility Plan · Prepared 2026</span>
      <h1>Leaf <em>&</em> Lantern</h1>
      <p class="plan-subtitle">An April-to-December Seasonal Gathering Place in Southeast Michigan</p>
      <p class="plan-thesis">
        Capital-disciplined. Seasonally productive. Built for return visits — and investor returns.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="container plan-layout">
    <nav class="plan-toc" aria-label="Plan sections">
      <span class="toc-title">Contents</span>
      <ol>
        {toc.map((t) => (
          <li><a href={`#${t.id}`} data-toc={t.id}>{t.label}</a></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <a class="btn btn-primary toc-cta" href={url('/')}>View the Concept Site</a>
    </nav>

    <article class="plan-body">
      <!-- ============ Executive Summary ============ -->
      <section id="summary" class="plan-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">01 · Executive Summary</span>
        <h2>A place people return to, season after season.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Leaf & Lantern is a seasonal gathering place built around rituals people already
          love: warm donuts, sweet cider, good coffee, changing landscapes, and time together.
          Autumn is the heart of the experience. Spring discovery, summer gathering, and
          holiday celebration give people reasons to come back.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="pull-quote">Autumn is our heart, not our entire calendar.</blockquote>
        <p>
          The business is deliberately focused. A short menu of excellent products drives
          everyday visits; the same hall, kitchen, and grounds support corporate retreats,
          school programs, camps, bulk orders, and standardized private gatherings across the
          calendar. No gate fee. No amusement sprawl. No bespoke event business.
        </p>
        <p>
          Leaf & Lantern begins by giving an existing place a new chapter. The preferred path
          is to acquire a character-rich church, lodge, school, farm structure, or similar
          property and adapt it within a <strong>≈$2.5–3.0M all-in capital envelope</strong>.
          Pilots come first; a permanent home follows only when food demand, retreat bookings,
          labor productivity, and the property economics have been proven.
        </p>

        <div class="metric-grid">
          {metrics.map((m) => (
            <div class="metric-card">
              <span class="metric-value">{m.value}</span>
              <span class="metric-label">{m.label}</span>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Concept & Mission ============ -->
      <section id="concept" class="plan-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">02 · Concept & Mission</span>
        <h2>Every season, a distinct purpose.</h2>
        <p>
          Leaf & Lantern is an April-to-December seasonal gathering place and food business
          focused on family traditions, local food, creative learning, community gatherings, and
          Michigan-made products. It does not need to operate as a large production farm, but its
          offerings remain materially connected to seasons, food, growing, making, and the
          landscape — never a generic rental hall temporarily decorated for different holidays.
        </p>
        <blockquote class="pull-quote">
          Leaf & Lantern seasonal experiences to enjoy traditions and the natural character of
          Michigan.
        </blockquote>

        <BrandImage
          src="/images/entrance-autumn.jpg"
          alt="The Leaf & Lantern arrival experience: cream hanging sign, stone bases, warm lanterns"
          ratio="21 / 9"
          class="plan-figure"
        />
        <p class="figure-note">
          Representative concept imagery; final architecture, signage, and branding may differ.
        </p>

        <h3>Operating principles</h3>
        <blockquote class="pull-quote">
          The investment thesis is a seasonal business made resilient through repeat visitation,
          disciplined operations, and productive reuse of the same property across the calendar.
        </blockquote>
        <p>
          The recommended structure is a for-profit operating company with the option of a
          separate property-holding entity. Educational partnerships may later justify a nonprofit
          partner, but the core business does not depend on grants to sustain ordinary operations.
        </p>
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table class="ll-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Principle</th><th>Business implication</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>Seasonally defined</strong></td><td>Every event fits Discovery, Gathering, Tradition, or Celebration.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Intimate rather than crowded</strong></td><td>Timed capacity and comfortable circulation take precedence over maximum attendance.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Food is central</strong></td><td>Cider, donuts, and coffee drive visitation; Leaf & Lantern supplies what it does exceptionally well and avoids building a catering operation.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Productive, not sprawling</strong></td><td>Every major space serves multiple revenue functions — retreats, camps, markets, private gatherings, and peak seating — without becoming a wedding venue or garden center.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Standardized, not bespoke</strong></td><td>Private gatherings are welcome only inside fixed packages; weddings, late-night events, and custom production remain excluded.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Local but edited</strong></td><td>Makers and products are selected for quality, utility, and fit.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Warm, not kitschy</strong></td><td>Natural materials, light, landscape, and real products rather than excessive props — a renovated place with character strengthens the brand.</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Lean until proven</strong></td><td>Opening payroll stays below mature levels; fixed overhead waits on demonstrated demand.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ Market ============ -->
      <section id="market" class="plan-section">
        <span class="eyebrow">03 · Market & Positioning</span>
        <h2>Familiar territory. Different philosophy.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Simply stated: <strong>preserve the seasonal emotion guests already want while systematically
          removing the friction, crowd dependence, and inconsistency that usually accompany it</strong> —
          and convert every season’s operating experience into measurable inputs for the next.
          Small, tested improvements outperform large speculative changes; complexity must
          justify itself; refinement targets the operation, never the tradition. That discipline
          explains decisions made throughout this plan: the simple hero menu, technology only
          where it removes friction, standardized programming instead of bespoke event hosting,
          adaptive reuse instead of ground-up construction, and a lean staffing model sized for
          proven demand rather than occasional peaks.
        </p>
        <div class="price-card">
          <span class="price-card-kicker">Site selection · screening tool</span>
          <p class="plan-tool-copy">
            Interactive screening of family demand, competition, and site fit across southeast
            Michigan.
          </p>
          <div class="price-card-cta">
