          The concept is worth pursuing; the permanent site is not yet a financeable conclusion
          on the numbers alone. The lowest-risk path validates demand through two full seasons of
          temporary programming — pop-up markets, a Halloween event, mobile cider-and-donut
          service, school pilots, corporate/retreat pilots, bulk-order tests, and rented-space
          holiday markets — before committing capital for an autumn 2030 opening. Pilots must
          answer whether Leaf &amp; Lantern can sustain a ≈$20+ food ticket, approach ~85k
          annual food transactions, and monetize retreats and bulk channels — inside a
          ≈$2.5–3.0M adaptive-reuse capital envelope with mature EBITDA above ≈$550–650k.
